{{ 'suntneew-a20-pdp.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

<section id="features" class="sn-a20-pdp sn-oj02-pdp" role="tabpanel" data-pdp-panel="features" aria-labelledby="oj02-experience-heading-{{ section.id }}">
  <div class="sn-a20-pdp__shell sn-a20-pdp__section">
    <p class="sn-a20-pdp__eyebrow">Features</p>
    <h2 class="sn-a20-pdp__heading" id="oj02-experience-heading-{{ section.id }}">Starting power with a diagnostic point of view.</h2>
    <p class="sn-a20-pdp__lede">OJ02 brings emergency starting, OBD2 diagnostics, device charging and roadside lighting into one compact tool for compatible 12V vehicles.</p>

    <div class="sn-a20-pdp__stack">
      <article class="sn-a20-pdp__feature">
        <picture class="sn-a20-pdp__feature-media"><img src="{{ 'suntneew-oj02-gallery-01-main.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="SuntNeew OJ02 OBD2 jump starter with accessories" width="2000" height="2000" loading="lazy"></picture>
        <div class="sn-a20-pdp__copy"><div><p class="sn-a20-pdp__eyebrow">OJ02 overview</p><h3>One tool for the start and the diagnosis.</h3><p>OJ02 combines a 12V jump starter with an OBD2 reader, a digital status display, USB output and three emergency light modes.</p></div><div class="sn-a20-pdp__metrics"><div class="sn-a20-pdp__metric"><strong>8,000mAh</strong><span>Rated capacity</span></div><div class="sn-a20-pdp__metric"><strong>29.6Wh</strong><span>Rated energy</span></div><div class="sn-a20-pdp__metric"><strong>1,500A</strong><span>Peak current</span></div><div class="sn-a20-pdp__metric"><strong>700A</strong><span>Starting current</span></div></div></div>
      </article>

      <article class="sn-a20-pdp__feature">
        <picture class="sn-a20-pdp__feature-media"><source media="(max-width: 749px)" srcset="{{ 'suntneew-oj02-feature-obd-mobile.jpg' | asset_url }}"><img src="{{ 'suntneew-oj02-feature-obd-desktop.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="SuntNeew OJ02 OBD2 diagnostic screen and vehicle connection" width="2400" height="1600" loading="lazy"></picture>
        <div class="sn-a20-pdp__copy"><div><p class="sn-a20-pdp__eyebrow">OBD2 diagnostics</p><h3>Read the vehicle before you decide what it needs.</h3><p>Use the built-in OBD2 system to read and clear fault codes, review live data and check supported vehicle information on compatible OBD2-equipped vehicles.</p></div><ul class="sn-a20-pdp__list" aria-label="OJ02 OBD2 functions"><li>9 diagnostic functions</li><li>9 major protocols</li><li>12 languages</li><li>Vehicle information</li></ul></div>
      </article>

      <article class="sn-a20-pdp__feature">
        <picture class="sn-a20-pdp__feature-media"><img src="{{ 'suntneew-oj02-feature-clamp.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="SuntNeew OJ02 connected to a compatible 12V vehicle battery with the smart clamp" width="1254" height="1254" loading="lazy"></picture>
        <div class="sn-a20-pdp__copy"><div><p class="sn-a20-pdp__eyebrow">Emergency starting</p><h3>Connect, check, start, then disconnect.</h3><p>Charge OJ02 to at least 50%, connect the EC5 clamp, attach red to positive and black to negative, and check the status light before starting a compatible 12V vehicle.</p></div><div class="sn-a20-pdp__utility"><div class="sn-a20-pdp__metrics"><div class="sn-a20-pdp__metric"><strong>6.0L</strong><span>Gasoline engine reference</span></div><div class="sn-a20-pdp__metric"><strong>3.0L</strong><span>Diesel engine reference</span></div><div class="sn-a20-pdp__metric"><strong>EC5</strong><span>Clamp interface</span></div><div class="sn-a20-pdp__metric"><strong>10AWG</strong><span>50cm smart-clamp cable</span></div></div><p class="sn-a20-pdp__steps-note">Follow the smart-clamp indicator and the full sequence in the OJ02 manual. Disconnect the clamp after the vehicle starts.</p></div></div>
      </article>

      <article class="sn-a20-pdp__feature sn-a20-pdp__feature--text">
        <div class="sn-a20-pdp__copy"><div><p class="sn-a20-pdp__eyebrow">Power, status and light</p><h3>The essential information stays visible.</h3><p>The screen shows remaining charge in 1% increments. A USB-A output supports compatible devices, while three LED modes cover routine illumination and roadside signaling.</p></div><div class="sn-a20-pdp__utility"><div class="sn-a20-pdp__metrics"><div class="sn-a20-pdp__metric"><strong>1%</strong><span>Charge display resolution</span></div><div class="sn-a20-pdp__metric"><strong>36W max</strong><span>USB-A output</span></div><div class="sn-a20-pdp__metric"><strong>5V / 9V / 12V</strong><span>USB-A output profiles, up to 3A</span></div><div class="sn-a20-pdp__metric"><strong>5V / 2A</strong><span>Type-C input</span></div></div><ul class="sn-a20-pdp__list sn-a20-pdp__list--three" aria-label="OJ02 light modes"><li>Steady</li><li>Warning flash</li><li>SOS</li></ul></div></div>
      </article>

      <article class="sn-a20-pdp__feature sn-a20-pdp__feature--text">
        <div class="sn-a20-pdp__copy"><div><p class="sn-a20-pdp__eyebrow">In the box</p><h3>The essential connections stay together.</h3><p>Store the unit, cables and manual in the supplied carrying pouch so the complete kit is easy to keep in the vehicle.</p></div><ul class="sn-a20-pdp__list" aria-label="OJ02 included components"><li>OJ02 main unit</li><li>50cm EC5 smart clamp</li><li>OBD connection cable</li><li>USB charging cable</li><li>English user manual</li><li>Carrying pouch</li><li>Retail box</li></ul></div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

